    "FILM_CORE is mandatory and may be made playable, but its order, participants and outcome do not change.",
    "FILM_EXPANDED adds interaction around a verified film scene without changing what the scene establishes.",
    "FILM_INTERSTITIAL is original gap-fill only between verified anchors and must close when the next film scene begins.",
    "BOOK_CHRONICLE is explicitly separated from the film timeline and may not silently become main-save canon.",
    "FUTURE_SOURCE_CHECK entries are ideas only, not runtime implementation authority.",
    "A film action should become gameplay before inventing a separate side quest for the same dramatic purpose."
  ],
  "audit_notes": [
    "The first film does not begin at Bilbo's birthday party: the prologue and Bilbo writing/Frodo-Gandalf opening precede the party.",
    "Tom Bombadil, Barrow-downs, Glorfindel-at-the-Ford and Scouring of the Shire are book-continuity material and must remain separately labeled Chronicles if used.",
    "The film continuity gives Arwen the Ford rescue role; a Glorfindel Chronicle cannot replace that main-film mission.",
    "The film continuity moves Shelob/Sam rescue into Return of the King; Part II must not import the book placement.",
    "Part III mission details remain FUTURE_SOURCE_CHECK until exact film/script scene-level verification is recorded in repository authority."
  ],
